styleScopeT -- inheritance, one rule (Tony, 2026-11-11, SEQ 623 R0, narrowing SEQ 622 R2): text properties inherit, box properties
do not, whether set as an attribute or in a style. Text: font, color, align, valign. Box: fill, border, strokeColor, rounded,
shadow, opacity. Rows in genLadder/formsPop.sh. SS-1 to SS-3: box properties stay on their field. SS-4, SS-5, SS-7: text properties
reach the children, from an attribute and from a held style (style:=). SS-6 pins a gap as it reads today: a style named by a quoted
name (style="x") is read by the fill and border floor but not by drawText. shadow's and opacity's own rows are in shadowT and opacityT.
The frames are written by hand and setFrame is not called.
